# Template for ~/.shell_local — machine-local environment + secrets.
# Copy to ~/.shell_local (chmod 600) and fill in your own values.
# NEVER commit ~/.shell_local. Sourced by ~/.shell_common; keep POSIX-compatible.
#
# On an existing machine, prefer copying the real file out of band:
#   scp othermachine:~/.shell_local ~/ && chmod 600 ~/.shell_local
#
# Put anything machine-specific or sensitive here: per-host env vars, API
# tokens, cloud credentials, private index passwords, personal path shortcuts,
# and host-only aliases. Each machine keeps only what it needs; nothing here has
# to match across machines.
#
# Examples (uncomment and replace with your own):
#   export MY_PROJECT_ROOT="$HOME/work"
#   export SOME_TOKEN="replace-me"
#   alias myq='some-command --user me'
